    "description": "Java/Progress 4GL Developer responsible for developing, unit testing, and supporting software projects throughout all phases of the software development life cycle for the SAIC’s Judicial Case Management System (Justech) Uniform Court System (UCS) business team in support of the Santa Clara County, California and State of Maryland Courts.\n\nImplemented and developed a JAVA (SOAP based) web service interface using HTTP(s) with SSL over TCP/IP to support the State of California’s Legal XML Second Generation Electronic Filing (EFiling)  Specifications (2GEFs) in order to implement an interface capability with the Uniform Court System (UCS), SAIC’s Judicial Case Management System.  Aided in WSDL development, XML to SQL Server database generation via Altova’s XML Spy and Interface development and testing. This was developed in J2EE Eclipse environment for a Tomcat server, using Maven builds and a SVN Repositories, Hibernate and a MS SQL Server database.\n\nImplemented upgrades to JAVA Web service in a (JAXB) interface for Progress to Oracle Database information Request/Reply exchange for Electronic Payments (Epayments) of Traffic tickets and Public Access of Traffic and Civil courts. This was developed in J2EE Eclipse environment for a Tomcat server, using Maven builds and a SVN Repositories.\n\nWorked collaboratively with court vertical teams (IT staff, Court Clerks, Operations Staff, External Agency Representatives, and Project Management) to develop and implement the specific technology and architecture necessary to deliver Court business solutions. \n\nCreated Excel Spreadsheet (Ecraft) with Visual Basic modules to maintain and export DoD Contract financial information in XML format for upload via Data Junction to an Oracle Database.  Assisted in the development of XML schema and DTD. Provided testing for Oracle PL/SQL algorithms present in the Oracle Database that processed the imported Excel Spreadsheet data.",
